{"reference":"Hosea 5","book":"Hosea","chapter":5,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A Historical Reading of the Crisis","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"One disputed historical reading understands the chapter’s alarms, royal leadership, and Ephraim’s appeal to Assyria for help as fitting the northern kingdom’s later eighth-century imperial crisis. On this reading, the appeal to a foreign king in verse 13 underscores the chapter’s portrayal of a crisis that human political help cannot heal.","verse_refs":["Hosea 5:1-15"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_hosea_005_8fa66efe489b3f474ab12721"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}